# x86 CLIENT desktop stack (thin) — appended onto packages.list for ROLE_CLIENT
# builds (laptop/chromebook/desktop). Mirrors the proven specs-frite light desktop
# (LXDE/openbox + lightdm) plus x86 laptop bits. The --desktop full weight adds
# packages-desktop-full.list on top. See docs/CLIENT-IMAGES.md.

# Display server + basic X utilities
x11-base/xorg-server
# Materializes the X drivers from INPUT_DEVICES (libinput: keyboard/mouse/touchpad)
# and VIDEO_CARDS (amdgpu/intel/nouveau DDX). Without it Xorg has no input/video
# driver and the greeter is unusable (modesetting/simpledrm still cover QEMU + UEFI
# fallback, but real touchpads/keyboards need xf86-input-libinput).
x11-base/xorg-drivers
x11-apps/xrandr
x11-apps/xset
x11-apps/setxkbmap
x11-terms/xterm

# Session: LXDE-lite — openbox WM + lxpanel + pcmanfm (lean, turnkey)
x11-wm/openbox
lxde-base/lxpanel
lxde-base/lxsession
x11-misc/pcmanfm
lxde-base/lxappearance

# Login / seat: lightdm + greeter + the OpenRC `display-manager` service
# (gui-libs/display-manager-init provides the service; lightdm ships none).
x11-misc/lightdm
x11-misc/lightdm-gtk-greeter
gui-libs/display-manager-init

# System bus + seat/login manager (enabled in the client runlevel)
sys-apps/dbus
sys-auth/elogind

# Networking UI + laptop power management
gnome-extra/nm-applet
sys-power/acpid

# Firewall — FD-06 superadmin shields-up uses firewalld; harmless on all clients
net-firewall/firewalld

# CPU microcode + firmware blobs (Intel/AMD laptops, wifi/bt firmware)
sys-firmware/intel-microcode
sys-kernel/linux-firmware

# Lean browser for the thin profile (full profile swaps in firefox/chromium)
www-client/netsurf

# Fonts + a file/image viewer + console editor
media-fonts/dejavu
media-fonts/noto
media-gfx/feh
app-editors/nano

# Desktop app governance (FD-09 increment 7 / admin-bff PR #115) — the
# admin-curated, domain-locked "Plasma Discover store" the keys-provision
# provision_desktop_governance() config targets. Discover is pointed at the
# admin-bff registry endpoint (a single Flatpak remote, Flathub removed, empty
# default) and installs governed apps as Flatpaks; without these packages the
# baked/USB-delivered #115 config has nothing to apply to.
#   sys-apps/flatpak       — the runtime the `flatpak remote` config + bearer-
#                            forward rely on (stable on amd64).
#   kde-plasma/discover    — the store front-end; USE=flatpak (package.use/desktop)
#                            builds its Flatpak backend → sys-apps/flatpak.
# DEP-WEIGHT NOTE: Discover is a Qt6/KF6 app and pulls the full Qt6 + KDE
# Frameworks 6 stack (qtbase/qtdeclarative/qtwebview + kconfig/kio/kirigami/…)
# onto this otherwise LXDE/openbox image — a material build-size/time increase.
# This is the lightest way to satisfy the design's "Plasma Discover" intent
# (the feature UI/contract is built around Discover specifically); no full
# Plasma desktop/meta package is added.
sys-apps/flatpak
kde-plasma/discover

# SSO-claim sudo runtime (increment 7's sudo leg — see docs/CLIENT-IMAGES.md).
# On a GOVERNED client image keys-provision strips sudoers/%wheel, so polkit is
# the ONLY escalation route and these two atoms are the whole runtime behind it:
#   sys-auth/polkit  — the authority that reads
#                      /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/49-hugmesh-desktop-sudo.rules (the
#                      default-deny addAdminRule gate) and resolves
#                      subject.isInGroup("desktop-sudo") through NSS at action
#                      time. Its duktape JS engine is unconditional and the
#                      image's global USE=elogind selects elogind session
#                      tracking (ConsoleKit is the no-elogind/no-systemd
#                      fallback and is NOT installed here). Today it arrives
#                      only as an lxde-base/lxsession dependency — declare it,
#                      because a session-manager swap must not silently take the
#                      governed image's sole sudo path with it.
#   dev-lang/python  — the interpreter for the desktop-sudo mapper:
#                      provision_desktop_governance() renders
#                      desktop-governance/sudo/desktop-sudo-mapper.py.tmpl to
#                      /etc/hugmesh/desktop-governance/desktop-sudo-mapper, a
#                      STDLIB-ONLY root cron (60s, base sys-process/cronie) that
#                      verifies each session's deposited OIDC token against the
#                      issuer JWKS and converges local `desktop-sudo` membership
#                      — the polkit gate's sole input. Stated contract, not an
#                      accident of portage's own python dependency.
# Nothing else is needed: membership is a LOCAL group, so nsswitch stays `files`
# and no PAM module is added.
#   Deliberately NOT sys-auth/sssd. Released SSSD has no generic-OIDC provider:
#   `id_provider = idp` (2.11.0, 2025-06-05) supports `idp_type` keycloak and
#   entra_id ONLY, reads users/groups over those products' REST APIs with its own
#   service client, authenticates via the RFC-8628 device-auth grant, and has no
#   token-claim->local-group mapping in any release through 2.13.1 — so it cannot
#   consume the per-domain Casdoor's deposited tokens. (The conf this mapper
#   replaced used `id_provider = oidc` + `oidc_groups_allowlist`: option names
#   that exist in NO release.) Gentoo's sssd is also ~amd64-only across every
#   version in tree, so shipping it would additionally need a keyword unmask for
#   a package that could not work here.
sys-auth/polkit
dev-lang/python

# ── Emulated-desktop display agent (QEMU runner --display spice) ──────────────
# When the containerised QEMU runner opens this image with a SPICE display, the
# native viewer (remote-viewer/spicy) resizes the GUEST to its window. The agent
# gives that session agent-mouse, clipboard and the XRandR path, and the
# session-side applier (/usr/libexec/hugmesh/vm-autofit, xdg autostart) applies
# the new preferred mode on a virtio-gpu/qxl hotplug — the lean LXDE session has
# no output daemon of its own. Both are inert on real hardware: the daemon is
# started by /etc/local.d/20-spice-vdagent.start ONLY when the SPICE virtio port
# exists (the stock OpenRC script fails red without it), and the applier exits
# at once unless the DRM driver is virtio_gpu or qxl.
#   app-emulation/spice-vdagent  — 0.22.1; USE=selinux (global) pulls the policy
#                                  module below, which the enforcing image loads
#                                  with every other installed .pp.
#   sec-policy/selinux-vdagent   — listed EXPLICITLY so the requested-atom
#                                  completeness gate asserts it installed; it is
#                                  stable on amd64 AND arm64 (2.20260616_p1), so
#                                  it needs NO keyword entry — and must not get
#                                  one (see the ARM keyword files).
app-emulation/spice-vdagent
sec-policy/selinux-vdagent
# Kernel side (specs-x86/kernel/desktop.config): CONFIG_VIRTIO_CONSOLE for the
# /dev/virtio-ports/com.redhat.spice.0 channel and CONFIG_INPUT_UINPUT for the
# daemon's /dev/uinput; CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU is already in hardened-k8s.config.
